[
    {
        "content": "<p>Suppose I'd like to write a parser that matches a number followed by an identifier, but only when then there is no whitespace between them.  For example, I'd like to match <code>37b</code> but not <code>37 b</code>.</p>\n<p>If I simply write <code>num</code> followed by <code>ident</code>, then Lean will match whether or not there is whitespace in between:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"abc\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"parsed\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">abc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">37</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"c1\">-- produces \"parsed\"</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">abc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">37</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- produces \"parsed\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is there some way to prevent the match when intervening whitespace is present?</p>",
        "id": 626923343,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1790350212
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That would be <code>noWs</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">noWs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"abc\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"parsed\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">abc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">37</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"c1\">-- produces \"parsed\"</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">abc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">37</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- error</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 626924761,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1790350523
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Excellent - that's just what I need.  Thanks for the lightning-quick reply!</p>",
